  "critique": {
    "axis": "clarity",
    "evidence": "The headline, explanatory copy, stage selector, selected-vector state, observable signals, and “Continue to scored replay” CTA establish a coherent map→inspect→score flow across viewports. However, desktop cards are visibly clipped on the left, the raw JSON is truncated on smaller screens, and the mobile/tablet header conceals later destinations behind an ambiguous “SWIPE” cue. The relationship between the kill-chain diagram, stage grid, and vector list also changes substantially by viewport without explanation.",
    "fix": "Eliminate card and JSON clipping, add an explicit horizontally scrollable/code affordance, preserve a clear active Atlas state in the compact header, and label the responsive stage grid as the kill-chain map so users understand that selecting a stage filters the vectors before continuing.",
